    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2995" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ăphăreus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ),
		ĕi, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀφαρεύς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of the Messenians;</i> hence his sons
			Lynceus and Idas are called
			Ăphărēïa proles, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8,
				304</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A centaur</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
				12, 341 sq.</span></i></div>
